        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "50a93cc1-93b0-5478-a65f-1816fc754c8a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Plant, John Bonham, Phil Collins, Nika Boon, John Baggott, Ian Matthews, Jay Stapley, Carey Willetts\n- Bands/Artists: Led Zeppelin, Massive Attack, Portishead, Kasabian, Pink Floyd, Mike Oldfield, Athlete\n- Events/Projects: Robert Plant tours, Nika Boon album\n\nFacts:\n- John Bonham was born on 31 May 1948 and became best known as the drummer for the British rock band Led Zeppelin.\n- John Bonham died on 25 September 1980.\n- Robert Plant avoided performing Led Zeppelin songs through much of that period.\n- Robert Plant's 1983 tour, with drummer Phil Collins, was very successful and often played to sold-out arena-sized venues.\n- Robert Plant's 1985 tour was very successful and often played to sold-out arena-sized venues.\n- Nika Boon was working on a new album for release in 2017.\n- Nika Boon's 2017 album involved collaboration with John Baggott, who played keyboard and moogs for Massive Attack, Portishead, and Robert Plant.\n- Nika Boon's 2017 album involved collaboration with Ian Matthews, the drummer from Kasabian, Jay Stapley, a guitarist associated with Pink Floyd and Mike Oldfield, and Carey Willetts, the bass player from Athlete.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
